# ASCENDKEEP — VISUAL STYLE BIBLE

Use the following visual direction consistently for every generated asset.

Dark fantasy minimalist 2D mobile game art, true top-down orthographic view, centered single subject, strong readable silhouette, compact proportions, slightly stylized hand-painted rendering, clean geometric shapes, restrained details, ancient stone and arcane energy aesthetic.

Color palette:

* near-black and deep navy shadows;
* desaturated stone gray;
* cyan and pale blue magical energy;
* muted antique gold for important details;
* violet energy for elite enemies;
* crimson only for danger, damage and corrupted states.

Lighting:

* soft light from directly above;
* subtle cyan magical rim light;
* controlled contrast;
* no dramatic background lighting;
* no realistic cast environment shadows.

Rendering:

* polished mobile game sprite;
* clean edges;
* subtle painted texture;
* no pixel art;
* no photorealism;
* no 3D render appearance;
* no excessive micro-details;
* readable at 64×64 pixels;
* transparent background;
* generous transparent padding around the subject.

Composition:

* one isolated subject;
* perfectly centered;
* entire object visible;
* no cropping;
* no scenery;
* no floor;
* no interface;
* no text;
* no border;
* no frame;
* no watermark.

The asset must visually belong to the same game as all other AscendKeep sprites.

NEGATIVE REQUIREMENTS:

Do not use an isometric perspective.
Do not use a side view.
Do not use a front-facing portrait view.
Do not add scenery or a painted background.
Do not add text, labels, numbers or interface elements.
Do not create cartoon comedy proportions.
Do not use bright saturated rainbow colors.
Do not use anime aesthetics.
Do not use photorealistic materials.
Do not create an elaborate illustration.
Do not crop the subject.
Do not add multiple objects unless explicitly requested.
